-- title:
--   Branch decomposition of the norm on R/xR for W[[U,V]]/(UV-varpi^e)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal. Let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, let $e \ge 1$ be a natural number, and write $R :=$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the ring $W[[U,V]]$ of two-variable formal power series (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \varpi^e$. Let $x \in R$ be nonzero and suppose $R/xR$ is a free and finite $W$-module. Then for every $r \in R$ the norm over $W$ of the class of $r$ in $R/xR$ — that is, the determinant of multiplication by that class as a $W$-linear endomorphism — equals the finitely supported product, over those prime ideals $Q$ of $R$ satisfying simultaneously $Q \ne 0$, $x \in Q$ and `const (ϖ ^ e) ϖ` $\notin Q$ (the class of the constant power series $\varpi$ does not lie in $Q$, i.e. $Q$ is horizontal), of the norm over $W$ of the class of $r$ in $R/Q$ raised to the power given by the natural number associated with the length, over the localisation of $R$ at $Q$, of the localisation of $R/xR$ at the complement of $Q$. Factors indexed by primes failing the three conditions are $1$, and `Algebra.norm` is taken in Mathlib's convention for algebras that need not be finite free.
--
--   This is the branch (horizontal-prime) decomposition of the norm form on the local crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^e)$ of a modular curve at a point where two branches meet, in the shape used to compute determinants of multiplication operators on $R/xR$ one branch at a time. The proof cites the decomposition of the norm of a finite algebra over a field into residue norms weighted by local lengths, and the statement in turn feeds the computation of leading residues of normalised coefficients in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.leadingResidue_nfCoeff_sSup_mul_finprod_residue_unitPart_norm_pow_eq_of_isUnit_coeff`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.leadingResidue_nfCoeff_sSup_mul_finprod_residue_unitPart_norm_pow_eq_of_isUnit_coeff).
-- source:
